WEBVTT

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:11.910
The tournament is a total
of three matches.

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:16.040
How would you fight them?

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:18.790
I'd try to minimize the
damage inflicted on me.

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:24.710
Even if I made it to the finals,
there'd be no point if I was all torn up.

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:27.840
I'd up my defense and have
my opponent try to hit me.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.090
And once they're exhausted...

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:34.930
...I'd look for an opening and counter.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:44.610
That's it. Don't underestimate
your distance.

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:52.030
Well, aren't you workin' hard...

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.990
Feel like you're fighting alongside him?

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.950
Like the good ol' days.

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:04.670
H-Hey, Joe!

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:07.210
Hey! Joe!

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:08.420
Joe!

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:18.470
Pops!

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.730
Why didn't you come?

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:32.650
Sachio, I--

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:35.780
It's all your fault that Pops died!

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:44.750
I'm never ever going to forgive you...

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:25.890
What? You can't read?

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:28.730
Oh, my bad. I forgot
immigrants can't read.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:31.810
No immigrants or 
stray dogs allowed!!

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:31.810
Local citizens

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:42.120
What're you looking at? We told you
to get lost, you stupid ol' hag!

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:46.750
Who do they think they are?

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:48.330
Stupid foreigners.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:51.380
If you've got a problem with this,
you can blame Chief!

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:54.250
Listen up.

00:03:54.250 --> 00:04:01.760
Don't you hold back. Make sure
you remind them who's boss.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:03.560
Just like him.

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:04.970
Yes, sir!

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:07.970
Leave, you stupid immigrants!!

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:09.770
Quit illegally occupying our land,
you vermin!!

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:14.520
"This isn't your home!
-Local citizens"

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:18.570
"Immigrants go home!"

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.780
This is awful.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:18.780
How can they be so cruel?

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:23.160
Don't worry about it. We just have to deal
with this until I win the tournament.

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:26.950
Come on, Chief. That's not
gonna make us feel any better.

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:30.080
This is all because you had
to go against Hikawa.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:33.250
Why don't we just make Joe
enter the tournament?

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:36.630
He came back, so now, we can
just apologize to Hikawa, and--

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:39.220
Joe's in no shape to fight.

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:42.300
Not to mention, this is <i>our </i>home!

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.640
If we don't face them ourselves,
we're gonna lose

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:47.180
something way more
important than our home.

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:50.730
Can you proudly live like that
in front of the kids?

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:53.940
He's right.

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:58.280
If we've got time to argue about this,
let's clean off all this graffiti.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:01.110
We're just gonna get thrown
out of here. What's the point?

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:03.570
Yeah, let's go.

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:14.330
It's not your fault.
Everyone's just on edge.

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:16.250
I know.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:19.010
Where's Joe?

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:21.180
He's fighting right now.

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:32.560
Joe's body is all messed up from the
shoddy painkillers he'd been taking.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:37.780
Until that crap's completely
out of his body,

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:40.280
he could experience pain at any time.

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:42.990
I guess that's what
happened with you, too.

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:47.910
Yeah. And it's only going to get worse.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:13.020
Were you able to get some sleep?

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:17.230
I'm sorry for bothering you like
this right before your match.

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:19.110
Nah.

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:22.780
I feel way more confident
having you around.

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:29.200
This is an herbal tea from our homeland.
It'll soothe any kind of pain.

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:37.210
That song you were just singing... You
were singing it when we first met, too.

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:44.130
"This is where you can come home to.
I'll be waiting for you."

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:47.390
It's a song from our homeland that
we sing to the souls of the dead.

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:51.060
Because the souls have lost their homes

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:54.890
and are fated to wander
the earth for eternity.

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:58.690
A place to come home to...

00:06:58.690 --> 00:07:00.980
You should have one, as well.

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:08.160
I destroyed that... along with
everything else with my own hands.

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:13.370
When my son died,
I thought the exact same thing.

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:20.880
I lost my homeland, but this is where...
my son and I can come home to.

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:23.340
And I'll be damned if I'm
gonna let anyone take it.

00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:32.560
It's finally begun! Our Town Festa
that only happens once a year!

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:36.560
The number in attendance the
first day is a new record high!

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:37.850
The event everyone is waiting for

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:42.150
is where eight contenders will
fight for the top cash prize...

00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:45.320
The Megalobox tournament!

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:49.160
The first block of matches
is about to begin!

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:52.200
Who will be the one to win
the top cash prize?!

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:00.290
Mr. Hikawa.

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:02.340
It really is him.

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:07.470
"Gearless" Joe. You seem
to have lost some weight.

00:08:07.470 --> 00:08:09.470
Let's go.

00:08:09.470 --> 00:08:12.430
Well, he was in a rotten mood, wasn't he?

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:21.020
Chief, you must feel great, having the
legendary champion as your second.

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:24.650
I sure do. I'm so nervous,
I might just piss myself.

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:29.530
I can't wait to see you lose
as pathetically as possible.

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:33.910
That asshole...

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:41.670
The rowdy commander from the shore...

00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:48.670
The Natural Born Destroyer...
Cannonball Maruyama!

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:50.300
And in this corner...

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:51.800
His opponent who overcame the rough seas

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:58.390
and hardships to get here from a
faraway land... The Real Boxer, Chief!

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:04.190
You don't belong here!

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:07.110
He surely must've meant Fake Boxer.

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:09.740
Chief, just do this as we practiced.

00:09:09.740 --> 00:09:11.820
Say, Joe...

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:16.910
Not a soul is expecting me to win.
Who could ask for better odds to bet for?

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:18.450
Yeah.

00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:38.930
What're you trying to
accomplish by staying here?

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:45.270
You just doing this on a whim?

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:48.940
Or are you trying to suddenly
act like a good person?

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:52.450
This ain't enough to make
your sins go away.

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:30.780
One round KO! The winner is Chief!

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:32.190
He secured a spot

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:36.030
to the second round in the tournament
with an unbelievable right hook!

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:43.370
Dirty immigrants

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:51.880
I heard from Chief that the locals
have been harassing you guys.

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:56.390
It's nothing new and it's nothing
for you to worry about.

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:01.010
You should be worrying about yourself.

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:04.020
Sorry, but I'm not hungry.

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:12.190
Then at least have some tea.

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:21.120
I heard that you're the one doing
maintenance on Chief's Gear.

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:22.200
Yup.

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:23.910
It's in great shape.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:28.130
It wasn't even phased despite how
much he got hit that last match.

00:11:28.130 --> 00:11:32.420
Well, that Gear...
Chief built that together with Carlo.

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:33.960
Carlo?

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:38.760
Chief's son. He was probably
around Mio's age now.

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:44.980
He lost his wife early on,
so it was just the two of them.

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:50.480
Apparently, he had always been frail.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:55.400
He lost him while they were
on the boat coming over here.

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:56.360
After that happened,

00:11:56.360 --> 00:12:01.990
Chief relied on alcohol and painkillers
as he stepped into the ring every night.

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:05.290
It was like he was punishing himself.

00:12:06.500 --> 00:12:10.580
I destroyed that... along with
everything else with my own hands.

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:14.550
When my son died, I thought
the exact same thing.

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:18.050
But one day, his Gear finally broke down.

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:22.100
And that was when Chief
finally broke down and cried

00:12:22.100 --> 00:12:24.640
for first time since Carlo had died.

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:28.940
Carlo had customized that Gear

00:12:28.940 --> 00:12:33.360
to specialize in defense
so that Chief wouldn't get hurt.

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:38.070
Chief felt like he had trampled
on his son's wishes.

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:41.410
That's what he told me as he cried.

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:46.620
That was the day that Chief changed.

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:52.000
He finally faced the true pain
he had been ignoring

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:55.750
and is now getting in that
ring to buy this land.

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:57.260
True pain...

00:12:57.260 --> 00:12:58.840
Yes.

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:02.390
And that's exactly why
Chief is going to win.

00:13:02.390 --> 00:13:04.930
At least, that's what I believe.

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:40.630
If you ever need anything, let me know.

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:42.630
Gracias.

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:45.970
That's a gift for you.

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:48.640
Thanks, Chief!

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:50.770
There's trouble!

00:13:50.770 --> 00:13:53.150
They got to our water supply pump!

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:00.990
Why would they go this far?

00:14:00.990 --> 00:14:04.780
They were waiting until we were
gone during the day to do this.

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:06.660
What are you gonna do about this, Chief?!

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:08.830
We told you this would happen!
This is your fault!

00:14:08.830 --> 00:14:11.660
We have children here!
How can they do this?

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:12.580
Say something!

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:14.460
Hey, Chief!

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:16.920
I'm gonna go grab some tools.

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:33.350
Did you really think you
could change like him?

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:35.440
Who do you think you are?

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:38.980
Did you really forget what you did?

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:43.400
I killed you...

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:47.870
That's right. You should've died instead.

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:54.210
Yeah. If I did, then I...

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:58.710
Then you wouldn't have had
to leave those kids behind?

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:00.670
Is that what you're trying to say?

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:03.130
Don't make me laugh.

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:06.180
This is your way of punishing yourself?

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:09.260
Do you really think you'll
be forgiven this way?

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:24.860
Let us help out, Chief.

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:26.160
You guys...

00:15:26.160 --> 00:15:30.580
This is our house. Let us do this.

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:31.700
Here, let me do it.

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:35.210
Come on, now. If you do it,
it still won't be fixed next year.

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:36.920
Oh, shut it. Just watch.

00:15:36.920 --> 00:15:38.000
Leave this to me.

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:40.130
Take a break.

00:15:40.130 --> 00:15:44.760
You can't keep dwelling on
the things you left behind.

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:48.720
Listen, Joe. It's all over.

00:15:48.720 --> 00:15:51.600
Is this really how it's going to end?!

00:15:56.890 --> 00:16:00.310
Now take these and feel better.

00:16:02.070 --> 00:16:09.110
Back there, Sachio asked me...
if this is really how it's going to end.

00:16:10.910 --> 00:16:16.160
I wanted to know the answer,
so I went to see you.

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:24.380
Please, Pops... I need you to
fight with me one more time.

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:33.390
So you can't even let me die in peace.

00:16:33.390 --> 00:16:35.350
Fine.

00:16:35.350 --> 00:16:39.730
My luck ran out the moment
I met you, anyway.

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:53.450
Say, Pops. Do you remember?

00:16:53.450 --> 00:17:01.500
The tiny light that I thought went out
ages ago hadn't gone out yet.

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:07.590
And I want to find out...
if it's just an illusion or not.

00:17:07.590 --> 00:17:08.590
It works!

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:10.590
So, please...

00:17:15.060 --> 00:17:19.850
I need you to fight with me one more time.

00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:49.110
Man, it sucks getting old.

00:18:49.110 --> 00:18:50.690
Chief.

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:52.690
You remember that match you had with me?

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:54.280
Of course.

00:18:54.280 --> 00:18:58.830
During that match, you acted like you
went down with my weak punch.

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:00.120
Yeah.

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:02.080
It's a longshot, but...

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:12.880
A punch is only effective
in these ten centimeters.

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:17.140
If it's any closer or farther away,
the impact goes down by half.

00:19:22.850 --> 00:19:26.520
You have the eye to
determine that distance!

00:19:30.650 --> 00:19:32.480
And he's down!

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:39.660
One! Two! Three! Four!

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:35.400
Chief!

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:39.660
I also have the acting skills to get
me an Oscar for best actor.

00:19:39.660 --> 00:19:41.240
That's it, Goro!

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:42.290
Get him!

00:19:42.290 --> 00:19:44.460
Six!

00:19:42.290 --> 00:19:44.460
Finish him off!

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:50.340
Seven! Eight! Nine!

00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:15.360
The winner is Chief!

00:20:15.360 --> 00:20:17.240
He did it!

00:20:19.070 --> 00:20:21.200
With a powerful blow to the left,

00:20:21.200 --> 00:20:24.540
the Real Boxer of the immigrants
has turned the tables with a KO

00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:27.750
and will be heading to the finals!

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:32.000
You filthy parasites...

00:20:41.180 --> 00:20:43.720
Do we really need to go this far?

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:48.850
Your job's not to think!
We just need to do what we're told.

00:20:50.400 --> 00:20:53.900
This is their own fault for
getting ahead of themselves.

00:20:53.900 --> 00:20:58.400
Don't worry. We're just gonna
give them a little scare.

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:03.530
Hey.

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:06.830
There you guys are. You guys
scribbling on the walls again?

00:21:08.250 --> 00:21:11.630
What the hell are those?
What are you trying to--

00:21:11.630 --> 00:21:13.170
Which side are you on?

00:21:13.170 --> 00:21:14.420
What?

00:21:14.420 --> 00:21:17.760
You're gonna do this with us,
aren't you? If you're one of us.

00:21:21.010 --> 00:21:24.100
I knew it. He's just one of them.

00:21:32.480 --> 00:21:34.310
Takubon, this is bad!

00:21:34.310 --> 00:21:35.860
Let's get the hell outta here!

00:21:42.530 --> 00:21:45.200
Carlo protected me again tonight.

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:48.500
Just remember, we still
have one more match.

00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:50.620
I'm not worried at all.

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:55.210
I have the best mechanic
and best second I could ask for.

00:21:57.170 --> 00:21:59.590
What? I can't enjoy a victory drink?

00:21:59.590 --> 00:22:02.590
I'll let you drink all you
want after this is over.

00:22:12.810 --> 00:22:13.900
What happened?!

00:22:13.900 --> 00:22:16.270
Hurry and get some water!

00:22:16.270 --> 00:22:18.270
Someone grab some buckets!

00:22:17.520 --> 00:22:19.360
Guys, we need your help!

00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:22.030
Chief, don't do it!

00:22:23.410 --> 00:22:24.740
Hey!
